# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#     The build context is what `docker build` uploads to the daemon and what any COPY in the
#     Dockerfile can reach. Two different things depend on this list.
#
#     **Nothing here may carry a secret.** The Dockerfile copies named paths rather than `.`,
#     so this list is the second lock rather than the only one - but a `.env` inside the
#     context is one careless `COPY . .` away from being a layer that cannot be deleted,
#     and an image layer is not a place a credential can be taken back out of.
#
#     **The context is also the build's cost.** `.venv/` and `.git/` are the two largest
#     directories in this repository and neither belongs in an image, so excluding them is
#     what makes the build fast enough to run repeatedly.
#
#     `docs/` is excluded for the first reason rather than the second: two of the files in it
#     are gitignored personal working documents (CLAUDE.md's note on
#     engineering-guidelines.md and interview-prep.md), and an image is a worse place to leak
#     them from than a repository.

# Version control
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Secrets, and anything shaped like one. `.env.example` is only a template, but the image has
# no use for it either, so the whole family stays out.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# The developer's virtual environment. The image builds its own from uv.lock, and this one
# holds Windows binaries that could not run in a Linux container anyway.
.venv
*.egg-info

# Bytecode and tool caches
__pycache__
*.pyc
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# The test suite. It is not runtime code, and it carries the harnesses, the recorded web
# responses and the fakes - none of which a production process may import.
tests

# Real-job measurement output: fetched third-party page text and report bodies (gitignored).
measurements

# Working documents, and the instruction file beside them. `docs/engineering-guidelines.md`,
# `docs/interview-prep.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are all gitignored local files, and a build context
# is sent whole to the daemon - which on a remote or shared builder is somewhere else
# entirely.
docs
CLAUDE.md

# Editor and OS files
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store

# The local infrastructure definition. Compose builds this image; the image does not run
# Compose.
docker-compose.yml
docker
